#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af05d3e-30eb-5918-91db-aa8c3a197237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257304} {:answer/id #uuid "3e616a32-d29b-5f08-93ed-071ac16b3da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257342} {:answer/id #uuid "7dce96d6-a180-5c14-a0e1-d3830ccaa2d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257895} {:answer/id #uuid "c144722c-9c7d-5454-80ab-16bbb5e3cf27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258472} {:answer/id #uuid "f753729a-b8ab-5b2d-bbfc-716c8a2bfb27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258949}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257342} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5d330ca-85d9-55ae-bc23-193deb6c6d8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "61d7ee8c-7043-59bf-884d-8cfd140d0d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-124237" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{2}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{bmatrix}$\n- ${T}_{3}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}2u+v \\\\ uv+1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6u+v \\\\ 4u+3v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only.\""}]}
